  "closureRetention": "Private closure records survive client/session retirement and expire only once all observations they reject are outside the existing 24-hour accepted range. A strictly newer accepted live ordering timestamp may also supersede its tab's fence because it rejects the same older events. Fences are omitted from public snapshots, share the existing saved-state byte budget, and cause explicit rollback/error if that budget is exceeded. No unexpired fence is evicted to make room. An ordinary transport disconnect does not close the source document.",
  "sourceClockContract": "Protocol-one remove accepts optional observedAt, validated against the same source-clock window as observations. New sensors send the actual removal clock; an older supplied removal cannot close a newer accepted document. Legacy callers that omit the field retain receive-time behavior. Automatic offline client/session retirement keeps only the last accepted source watermark, rather than inventing a newer provider timestamp from receive time. Dedicated failing-before/passing-after regressions cover delayed delivery and immediate valid new documents.",
